From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:46:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: dispatch extendable service-worker message events

Add a native service-worker-only ExtendableMessageEvent derived from
ExtendableEvent, including factory/subtype/bridge plumbing, constructor
message fields and defaults, and frozen ports arrays. Preserve ordinary
MessageEvents and interface exposure in dedicated/shared workers and pages.
Constructor data remains local until all dictionary conversion and native
allocation succeed, so invalid later fields cannot root a failed payload.

Dispatch service-worker message and messageerror with the new interface and
existing structured-cloned payloads. Each dispatched message has an independent
intrusive retained owner for its native event and JS wrapper, separate from the
single lifecycle slot. Seal even interrupted dispatch, release only after every
accepted lifetime promise settles, and keep other overlapping messages alive
when one promise fulfills or rejects. Release cloned data on scheduling and
event-creation failures as well as queued-task cancellation.

Reuse ExtendableEvent promise tracking with Promise<any> conversion for values
and thenables. Check trust and active state after conversion, including a
reentrant then getter that settles the last old promise during a nested
microtask checkpoint. Synthetic events and first late calls without pending
promises reject with InvalidStateError; additional calls while promises remain
pending can extend the event. Preserve existing install/activate ordering and
lifecycle rejection behavior.

On worker teardown cancel lifecycle/message completion callbacks before
context disposal, retain native pointers until callbacks/tasks have been
disabled, then release all independent owners exactly once.

Validation:
- scripts/build.sh: release build passed after review fixes.
- scripts/build.sh build-dev: debug build passed after review fixes.
- scripts/build.sh test: all 1658 existing tests passed unchanged.
- Ignored localhost HTTP/CDP fixtures with serviceworker explicitly enabled:
  constructor defaults/options, Event/ExtendableEvent prototype chain, frozen
  ports, synthetic waitUntil restrictions, MessagePort constructor source,
  interface absence in Window/dedicated/shared workers and unchanged ordinary
  worker MessageEvents passed.
- Queued-before-load cloned object snapshots and string delivery, overlapping
  message lifetimes with multiple promises, rejection isolation, GC retention,
  adding promises while pending, late-call rejection (including first microtask
  calls), thenable/primitive conversion, install/activate/claim all passed.
- Reentrant thenable conversion rejects after the previous lifetime ends;
  failed constructor payloads are collectible across GC. Both review findings
  addressed and covered by temporary diagnostics, with no new upstream tests.
- Release and debug runs passed unresolved-promise teardown, 12 repeated pending
  message closures, queued-message cancellation and navigation; no browser
  errors, assertions or crashes. Diagnostics remain ignored and uncommitted.
- One reviewer pass completed, both findings fixed, builds/tests and affected
  diagnostics rerun. No benchmark changes or persona/default-feature changes.

Boundary: sender source stays null and origin stays empty for delivered
messages until the separate Client/reply patch. No transferable transport,
client replies, fetch interception, persistence or background restart. Existing
creating-Page worker ownership and simplified lifecycle behavior remain. No
benchmark success or complete service-worker API conformance is claimed.

Specification references:
https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#extendablemessageevent-interface
https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#wait-until-method
https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#service-worker-postmessage
